{
  "_about": "EV-011 cases for plan kensaku-v1-1: v1.1 classification additions (CR-002 search and category pages, editorial paths and hosts, second-hand marketplaces, SG aggregators, unambiguous currency symbols). Live cases reference real Exa responses: V2/V3/V5/V7 from the kensaku-v1-1 pre-approval spike (2026-11-21) and R1-Q5/R1-Q6 copied byte-for-byte from the EV-008 run 1 log. Synthetic cases (Z01-Z16) are labeled synthetic.",
  "labelStatus": "Assistant-proposed labels computed by a reference implementation of the written rules in docs/futari/ARCHITECTURE.md 'Offer classification' (independent of src/core), reviewed case by case. They become gold labels only when the owner approves plan kensaku-v1-1. They describe Kensaku's rules applied to Exa's extracted data, not independent truth about the pages.",
  "ruleAdditions": {
    "4": "Aggregator list gains kiasuprice.com and priceme.com (host or any subdomain).",
    "5": "Editorial list gains aboutamazon.com, aboutamazon.jp, androidcentral.com, note.com, hardwarezone.com.sg.",
    "7": "Before the three-letter check, a trimmed currency equal to one of these exact strings is mapped: 'S$' and 'SG$' -> SGD; 'US$' -> USD; '¥', '￥', '円', 'JP¥' -> JPY. A bare '$' and every other string are unchanged (so '$' stays invalid).",
    "5a": "New, after rule 5: host on the second-hand marketplace list (carousell.sg, carousell.com, jp.mercari.com, auctions.yahoo.co.jp) -> evidence: marketplace.",
    "5b": "New, after 5a: the hostname's first label is exactly 'search', or any path segment (percent-decoded, lowercased) is one of search, s, category, categories, bestsellers, productlist, or a 'collections' segment is not followed later by a 'products' segment -> evidence: search-or-category. Applies even when Exa reports isProductListing true.",
    "5c": "New, after 5b: any path segment is one of news, blog, blogs, review, reviews, article, articles -> evidence: editorial."
  },
  "supersedes": {
    "L29": {
      "expected": {
        "outcome": "evidence",
        "category": "editorial"
      },
      "was": {
        "outcome": "evidence",
        "category": "merchant-mismatch"
      },
      "rationale": "Rule 5c: hothardware.com/news/... is a news article; it was evidence before and stays evidence, only the category changes (D-031)."
    },
    "Y03": {
      "expected": {
        "outcome": "merchant-offer",
        "currency": "USD",
        "amount": 278
      },
      "was": {
        "outcome": "evidence",
        "category": "merchant-no-price"
      },
      "rationale": "Rule 7 amendment: 'US$' now maps to USD (D-032). Z05 keeps the invalid-currency coverage with a bare '$'."
    }
  },
